Rule 1 (out, when provided, must be a Tensor with the exact Kronecker output shape)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ ndim(v_2) = ndim(v_3) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) > 0 ∧ shape(v_2, i) > 0 ∧ shape(v_3, i) = shape(v_1, i) * shape(v_2, i)
>>
Rule 2 (avoid excessive allocation by bounding per-dimension growth and total rank)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ ndim(v_1) ≤ 6 ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) > 0 ∧ shape(v_2, i) > 0 ∧ shape(v_1, i) * shape(v_2, i) ≤ 1048576
>>
Rule 3 (align dtypes across inputs and out to prevent invalid casts)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) = dtype_(v_2) ∧ dtype_(v_3) = dtype_(v_1)
>>
Rule 4 (when not using out, keep inputs’ dtypes aligned to avoid unintended casting)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) = dtype_(v_2)
>>
Rule 5 (allow different ranks only if one operand is a scalar)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) ≠ ndim(v_2) then (ndim(v_1) = 0 ∨ ndim(v_2) = 0)
